# Work & project media assets

## Default workflow

1. **You drop finished assets** into `public/images/work/{slug}/` (or project media folders). Prefer RGBA WebP with browser chrome + drop shadow and a transparent mat — same as existing work thumbs (e.g. Care Continuity).
2. **Agent only wires paths** in frontmatter / components. Do not invent or “fix” images from CleanShot RGB-on-black exports.

## Naming (required)

| File | Role |
|------|------|
| `gallery-01.webp` | Lead stage image **and** card `thumbnail` |
| `gallery-01.png` | **Open Graph** (`og:image`) — same art as `gallery-01.webp` |
| `gallery-02.webp`… | Remaining gallery shots |

Frontmatter pattern:

```yaml
thumbnail: "/images/work/{slug}/gallery-01.webp"
gallery:
  - "/images/work/{slug}/gallery-02.webp"
  - "/images/work/{slug}/gallery-03.webp"
```

Work pages already map a `.webp` thumbnail → sibling `.png` for Open Graph. When wiring a new/updated entry, if `gallery-01.webp` exists and `gallery-01.png` does not, make a **lossless** WebP→PNG copy of gallery-01 only (OG requirement). No other image processing.

## Do not

- Black-mat punching, cropping, resizing, chrome compositing, synthetic shadows, or bulk format conversion
- Point `thumbnail` at a separate `thumbnail.png` when `gallery-01` exists — gallery-01 is the thumb
